In C programming, you can terminate a program using the `exit()` function from the `stdlib.h` library. This function causes the program to terminate and returns a status to the operating system. Here is an example of how you might use it:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Program is about to terminate.\n");
    exit(1);  // This will terminate the program and return status 1 to the OS.
}
```

